      "analysis_status": "completed",
      "threat_classification": "T1110 - Brute Force & T1548.003 - Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism: Sudo and Sudo Caching",
      "executive_summary": "An adversary conducted multiple SSH authentication brute-force attempts from external source IPs against the host. Following successful brute-force logins for user accounts, privileged command executions via sudo were performed, including spawning interactive root shells and modifying critical web directory permissions.",
      "attack_scenario": "The incident began with repeated SSH authentication failures from source IP 198.51.100.61 targeting the root user, followed by brute-force password guessing against user_419 and user_472 from IPs 203.0.113.29 and 203.0.113.182 respectively, culminating in successful logins. Subsequently, user 'ubuntu' executed interactive root shells via sudo (/bin/bash) and modified file permissions on the web directory (/bin/chmod 777 /var/www/html).",
      "risk_level": "high",
      "risk_score": 85,
      "confidence_level": "high",
      "confidence_reason": "Direct authentication logs and sudo execution logs explicitly capture the brute-force sequence and subsequent privileged command execution.",
